   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to the\nestablishment and priorities of the New York state council on hunger and food\npolicy",
    "basePrintNo": "S829",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S829-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §16, Ag & Mkts L (as proposed in S.549-B & A.3954-B)",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S829\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to the\nestablishment and priorities of the New York state council on hunger and\nfood policy\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.645.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by expanding the purpose\nof the council to include hunger along with food policy. This chapter\namendment increases the council size to 25 members, modifies member\nappointments, and requires the council to meet at least twice a year.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 29 of 2022, the Executive and Legislature\nreached this agreement to build on the work of the existing Council on\nHunger and Food Policy by codifying it and expanding the priorities of\nthe Council.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 645 of the Laws of 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the Agriculture and Markets Law and\nEconomic Development Law relating to procurement of locally grown farm\nand food products and codifying the New York State council on food poli-\ncy, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.549-B and A,3954-B, takes\neffect.\n",
